Third-party material
--------------------

Some marks in the own icons under src/own/ come from, or are redrawn after,
Material Symbols by Google.

  Project:  Material Symbols (google/material-design-icons)
  Upstream: https://github.com/google/material-design-icons
  Files:    symbols/web/<symbol>/materialsymbolsrounded/<symbol>_fill1_24px.svg
  Revision: 10ecc14790612ca8fd164e3f4ffe9c16fc50d5b7 (2026-10-23)
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0
            https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
            The full text is at the end of this file.

Changes made to the upstream files: path data was scaled and moved from the
960-unit Material canvas onto the Dux Icons 24-unit grid, rounded to two
decimals, placed on a folder, a document sheet or the tile itself, and its
fill replaced by the build tokens @glyph, @tile and @back. Nothing else from
upstream is shipped.

